WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:30.750
ClassicaLoid So Far

00:02.980 --> 00:04.790
Tenants wanted!

00:05.230 --> 00:08.190
I'm the landlady at Otowakan, Otowa Kanae.

00:08.630 --> 00:12.650
I have a few weird freeloaders
living here, but don't mind them.

00:12.650 --> 00:15.100
They have the same names
as famous composers,

00:15.100 --> 00:17.240
and they play strange music,

00:17.240 --> 00:19.440
and they burn the room frying gyoza,

00:19.440 --> 00:21.490
and they run down the
hallway on roller shoes,

00:21.490 --> 00:23.520
and we get attacked by enemies and stuff,

00:23.520 --> 00:25.660
but it's an amazing home.

00:25.660 --> 00:28.250
But please be sure to pay your rent.

00:28.580 --> 00:30.520
Feel free to come for a tour!

00:34.580 --> 00:35.900
Magnificent.

00:36.630 --> 00:37.720
Here,

00:38.060 --> 00:38.970
here,

00:39.470 --> 00:40.350
there,

00:40.720 --> 00:41.850
everywhere...

00:42.110 --> 00:44.350
It's absolutely magnificent!

00:44.680 --> 00:47.890
It's great when someone <i>gets</i> it, you know?

00:47.890 --> 00:49.590
How valuable this mansion is.

00:49.590 --> 00:50.990
I'm impressed,

00:51.860 --> 00:53.350
uh...

00:53.350 --> 00:54.420
Who were you, again?

00:54.420 --> 00:55.530
Schubert.

00:55.530 --> 00:58.340
A man who adores Beethoven-senpai
more than any other.

00:58.340 --> 00:59.530
Schubert.

00:59.530 --> 01:00.670
Oh, right.

01:00.670 --> 01:04.210
You're Schu-san. You showed up out of
nowhere after that huge fuss the other day.

01:04.210 --> 01:06.250
I thank you from the bottom of my heart

01:06.250 --> 01:09.130
for the opportunity to live here, Landlady.

01:09.390 --> 01:12.880
For Beethoven-senpai lives here!

01:12.880 --> 01:13.880
Magnificent!

01:14.560 --> 01:16.950
Even this run-down,

01:16.950 --> 01:19.890
undermaintained mess is
heaven, if Senpai is here!

01:20.380 --> 01:23.390
Please be sure to pay your rent.

01:25.290 --> 01:26.340
Rent?

01:27.200 --> 01:29.320
Speaking of which, where is Senpai?

01:29.320 --> 01:31.510
I haven't seen him these past few days.

01:31.510 --> 01:33.650
Senpai!

01:34.980 --> 01:36.080
You, too?

03:07.620 --> 03:10.240
Stop it. Do you need to film?

03:10.240 --> 03:12.230
Come on, it's our first date.

03:12.230 --> 03:13.750
And our first hike.

03:13.750 --> 03:14.960
What's that?

03:15.780 --> 03:16.600
Huh?

03:16.600 --> 03:18.380
Look at those rocks.

03:18.380 --> 03:19.670
Is it a ritual or something?

03:19.670 --> 03:21.450
It's kind of creepy.

03:21.450 --> 03:23.770
Hey, there's more over there, too.

03:24.600 --> 03:27.170
What the hell is this?

03:27.170 --> 03:29.600
Hey, let's go back.

03:30.810 --> 03:31.900
What is this?

03:31.900 --> 03:32.900
This is bad.

03:32.900 --> 03:34.330
Let's go home.

03:37.980 --> 03:39.420
Oh, crap. Oh, crap!

03:39.420 --> 03:41.150
Wait, I can't take it!

03:41.860 --> 03:45.610
I'm sorry! You're not supposed
to enter forbidden mountains.

03:45.610 --> 03:49.900
I'm sorry, Mom, Dad!

03:49.790 --> 03:54.250
07: "Mountain King"

03:49.900 --> 03:53.510
This footage was obtained
exclusively for this program.

03:50.370 --> 03:53.170
You couldn't get any more fake.

03:53.510 --> 03:55.830
The woman has since returned to safety.

03:54.550 --> 03:56.420
Are you into this stuff?

03:55.830 --> 03:58.420
Nothing out of the ordinary
has been reported.

03:58.420 --> 04:05.800
Terror!! Hamamatsu Urban Legend

03:58.670 --> 04:01.660
Just what did they see in the mountains?

04:01.660 --> 04:04.110
What was it that chased them?

04:04.530 --> 04:05.800
Here's the footage.

04:05.800 --> 04:06.050
Terror!!

04:05.800 --> 04:06.050
Hamamatsu Urban Legend

04:06.050 --> 04:12.480
Terror!!
Hamamatsu Urban Legend

04:07.080 --> 04:09.750
We have named this creature the Hamagon,

04:08.310 --> 04:08.810
Hamagon

04:08.810 --> 04:09.060
Hamagon
Length: 180cm?

04:09.060 --> 04:12.480
Hamagon
Length: 180cm?
Weight: 70 kg?

04:09.750 --> 04:12.040
and we intend to continue
research in the future.

04:12.970 --> 04:14.660
Is it just me,

04:14.660 --> 04:17.270
or does that thing look familiar?

04:17.270 --> 04:18.020
It's...

04:18.020 --> 04:18.840
"It's"?

04:19.430 --> 04:22.220
It's the Forest King.

04:22.650 --> 04:25.390
Wait, it's not the <i>Forest</i> King.

04:26.160 --> 04:28.490
It's the Forest King!

04:28.920 --> 04:31.020
Tchaiko-chan?

04:44.520 --> 04:45.260
Poot.

04:45.570 --> 04:48.190
You got me!

04:48.190 --> 04:49.410
Take this!

04:49.410 --> 04:50.230
Poot!

04:50.230 --> 04:51.410
Pee-yew!

04:51.410 --> 04:52.680
Poot.

04:55.670 --> 04:57.940
My dear boy...

05:01.930 --> 05:03.130
Maman.

05:08.650 --> 05:10.440
Such a nice day.

05:10.440 --> 05:11.910
You mustn't, my little kitten.

05:12.230 --> 05:14.340
UV rays are bad for your skin.

05:14.640 --> 05:16.710
Don't let your guard down
just because you're young.

05:16.930 --> 05:18.540
Y-Yeah?

05:18.540 --> 05:19.710
Use this.

05:19.710 --> 05:21.710
Nah, I have to clean.

05:22.010 --> 05:24.240
Oh, dear.

05:24.240 --> 05:26.490
Don't be shy. This is love.

05:26.490 --> 05:27.300
Love.

05:27.300 --> 05:29.100
Thank you.

05:30.990 --> 05:33.300
It's kind of quiet today.

05:33.300 --> 05:35.280
Because Beethes and Motes aren't here.

05:35.280 --> 05:36.350
They aren't?

05:36.650 --> 05:37.990
Senpai is here.

05:37.990 --> 05:38.690
Huh?

05:38.990 --> 05:41.190
The great Beethoven-senpai has

05:41.190 --> 05:44.190
cloistered himself to
pursue greater heights.

05:44.190 --> 05:46.230
Greater heights?

05:46.230 --> 05:46.860
Yes.

05:46.860 --> 05:49.410
Don't Open!

05:47.310 --> 05:49.840
New inspiration bubbling within him.

05:49.840 --> 05:53.290
The concentration to capture
it and ruminate on it.

05:53.600 --> 05:56.970
A gaze of solitude, allowing
none to approach him.

05:57.270 --> 06:00.540
Every breath he takes, every move
he makes, is the work of a genius.

06:00.910 --> 06:03.300
So what's Beethes doing?

06:05.690 --> 06:09.340
Mere mortals like you may
neither see nor speculate.

06:09.340 --> 06:11.090
You don't know, either, do you?

06:11.090 --> 06:13.310
That's not the point!

06:13.310 --> 06:16.430
The point is that you mustn't get
in the way of his ascension!

06:15.720 --> 06:16.430
Where's Motes?

06:19.610 --> 06:23.460
I know nothing of that trite man.

06:23.460 --> 06:26.940
He may have fallen into a
river chasing a butterfly,

06:27.270 --> 06:30.270
or he may be spinning around in public,

06:30.270 --> 06:31.910
mouthing crude jokes.

06:31.910 --> 06:36.580
That man doesn't even deserve
to be in the same room as a true artist.

06:32.490 --> 06:35.440
I mean, as long as he's safe.

06:35.760 --> 06:36.830
Kanae!

06:37.310 --> 06:39.240
Did you see the special yesterday?

06:39.240 --> 06:40.370
Wasn't that Motes-san?

06:40.730 --> 06:41.990
This thing.

06:41.990 --> 06:43.420
That's totally Motes-san.

06:44.360 --> 06:47.000
What has that guy gone and done?

06:47.000 --> 06:48.390
Let's go check it out.

06:48.390 --> 06:50.840
So we're meeting up over there, right?

06:52.510 --> 06:53.930
Kanae.

06:53.930 --> 06:56.540
Man, the weather's so nice today.

06:56.540 --> 06:58.160
I think I'll hang the futons.

06:58.160 --> 07:00.220
Aren't you at least <i>slightly</i> interested?

07:00.220 --> 07:04.460
Let her enjoy this peace
a little longer, tool.

07:07.140 --> 07:11.060
How am I going to keep up being a landlady
if I keep sweating the little stuff?

07:14.530 --> 07:16.450
Did you see <i>Hamamatsu
Urban Legends</i> yesterday?

07:16.770 --> 07:17.530
I did.

07:17.530 --> 07:18.350
Hamagon!

07:18.350 --> 07:20.360
Hey, let's go check it out after school.

07:20.360 --> 07:22.370
It sounds fun, Kanae.

07:22.710 --> 07:23.690
It's a tengu.

07:23.690 --> 07:24.670
Huh?

07:25.090 --> 07:26.910
It isn't Hamagon.

07:26.910 --> 07:27.990
It's a tengu.

07:28.390 --> 07:30.920
Mess with it, and it'll take you away.

07:31.470 --> 07:34.360
No, I think you're taking it too seriously.

07:34.900 --> 07:36.940
That Hamagon, though.

07:36.940 --> 07:38.390
Let's go catch it.

07:38.390 --> 07:40.600
It's all about that Hamagon.

07:40.600 --> 07:43.210
No! No! I want to go see Hamagon.

07:43.210 --> 07:44.100
You may not.

07:44.100 --> 07:45.920
Why not?

07:44.790 --> 07:46.840
He's a huge buzz.

07:46.840 --> 07:48.890
He's annoying when he's at home.

07:48.890 --> 07:51.940
He causes problems when he's out.

07:52.240 --> 07:53.360
So are you just going to leave him?

07:53.660 --> 07:55.800
I'm just a landlady.

07:55.800 --> 07:58.620
I'm not responsible for what
my tenants do outside.

07:58.840 --> 08:01.010
But, like, what if someone

08:01.010 --> 08:03.000
ends up capturing him?

08:04.620 --> 08:05.880
Capturing?

08:06.510 --> 08:11.170
Kanae! Kanae!

08:09.460 --> 08:11.380
<i>Who's Kanae?</i>

08:11.380 --> 08:13.720
The girl from that mansion, I heard.

08:14.660 --> 08:17.600
What is your relationship with Hamagon?

08:17.600 --> 08:19.370
Are you Hamagon, too?

08:19.370 --> 08:21.350
I'm not. I'm not!

08:21.650 --> 08:23.330
Look, it's that girl.

08:23.330 --> 08:24.490
The Hamagon girl.

08:25.080 --> 08:26.230
Did you hear?

08:26.450 --> 08:28.610
So disgraceful for such a young girl.

08:28.610 --> 08:29.930
I know.

08:30.230 --> 08:34.110
Hamagon Get Out

08:30.230 --> 08:34.110
Back to the Mountains

08:30.560 --> 08:32.940
Go back to the mountains, Hamagon!

08:32.940 --> 08:34.110
Go back!

08:34.540 --> 08:36.620
You're a menace to public discipline!

08:36.620 --> 08:38.640
Menace!

08:39.550 --> 08:40.550
What's up?

08:40.550 --> 08:42.720
I'm worrying too much.

08:48.560 --> 08:49.800
Beethes.

08:50.090 --> 08:51.680
Come on, Beethes.

08:52.170 --> 09:01.560
Don't Open!

08:52.400 --> 08:53.750
You're in there, aren't you?

08:53.750 --> 08:54.970
Beeth—

08:53.930 --> 08:55.690
It's gone!

08:55.690 --> 08:56.780
I-I'm sor—

08:56.780 --> 08:57.900
Sound, raining from above.

08:57.900 --> 08:59.850
I hear it! No, I see it!

08:59.850 --> 09:02.990
Straight lines, curved lines...
Gone! Once More!

09:01.820 --> 09:04.890
I'm sorry. So hey, Motes is
hiding in the mountains.

09:04.890 --> 09:06.790
There's a bit of a commotion.

09:06.790 --> 09:09.550
I was wondering if you could
do something about it.

09:12.320 --> 09:14.340
Hee, hee, hoo.

09:14.710 --> 09:16.560
Hee, hee, hoo.

09:16.560 --> 09:17.990
Not even listening.

09:16.560 --> 09:18.890
Hee, hee, hoo.

09:18.300 --> 09:20.540
Beethes! Hey, Beethes!

09:19.260 --> 09:20.990
Hee, hee, hoo.

09:23.000 --> 09:26.960
How refreshing it is without
that low-life around.

09:27.500 --> 09:30.370
We all ought to just
pretend he never existed,

09:30.370 --> 09:32.780
and live a peaceful life.

09:32.780 --> 09:33.840
Yeah.

09:44.140 --> 09:45.840
Y-You're...

09:50.610 --> 09:54.400
Th-That's my snack for Beethoven-senpai!

09:57.190 --> 09:59.450
Help me!

10:01.890 --> 10:02.980
Hamagon!

10:02.980 --> 10:03.950
Seriously?

10:03.950 --> 10:06.390
Help me!

10:08.060 --> 10:09.540
I lose.

10:09.800 --> 10:12.350
I can't beat Beethes' concentration.

10:13.630 --> 10:14.930
It's from Cho-chan.

10:15.810 --> 10:17.980
Motes, or I guess, Hamagon,

10:17.980 --> 10:20.050
is prowling the streets.

10:20.260 --> 10:21.050
What?!

10:21.450 --> 10:23.560
Apparently there're videos online.

10:23.560 --> 10:25.560
Shocking footage! We saw Hamagon on the streets!
610 views

10:24.140 --> 10:27.810
Somebody help me!

10:28.200 --> 10:30.550
This is our neighborhood.

10:30.550 --> 10:31.560
Let go!

10:32.610 --> 10:36.610
I will deliver this gyoza to
Senpai, even if it kills me.

10:42.370 --> 10:44.440
Hey, what are you two—

10:44.440 --> 10:45.550
Look at that!

10:45.870 --> 10:47.350
Isn't that Hamagon?

10:47.350 --> 10:48.620
Why is it at this mansion?

10:47.630 --> 10:48.620
No way!

10:50.980 --> 10:52.670
It's nothing!

10:52.920 --> 10:55.530
Kanae, Motes is in the mansion.

10:57.060 --> 10:58.630
Tender.

10:59.420 --> 11:00.860
Tense.

11:01.880 --> 11:02.630
No...

11:02.970 --> 11:05.420
Motes, what's wrong with you?

11:05.420 --> 11:06.750
Stop it, Motes.

11:06.750 --> 11:07.470
Damn it, Motes!

11:07.760 --> 11:09.750
Yes, Motes...

11:11.250 --> 11:11.980
Motes?

11:13.460 --> 11:13.900
Motes.

11:16.240 --> 11:17.650
Motes?

11:20.420 --> 11:21.410
Huh?

11:21.820 --> 11:23.370
Maman!

11:24.380 --> 11:28.870
Maman!

11:31.360 --> 11:32.330
I saw it.

11:32.330 --> 11:33.240
Motes?

11:33.840 --> 11:34.780
No...

11:35.080 --> 11:37.480
Inspiration.

11:45.560 --> 11:47.810
Why did Hamagon

11:47.810 --> 11:50.070
appear in town?

11:50.070 --> 11:53.310
It appeared to have vanished
into the mountains soon after.

11:53.310 --> 11:58.360
Hamagon Sighted in Town!!
Follow-up!!

11:53.650 --> 11:55.760
We continue our research in hopes of

11:55.760 --> 11:58.820
uncovering the truth as soon as possible.

11:59.580 --> 12:02.030
Why was he screaming "Maman"?

12:02.030 --> 12:03.210
Maman?

12:03.210 --> 12:04.860
His mother, perhaps?

12:04.860 --> 12:06.060
Mother?

12:06.060 --> 12:09.790
In any case, we need to
deal with that idiot.

12:09.790 --> 12:12.370
My little kitten's getting sicker and sicker.

12:11.790 --> 12:13.020
Forget it.

12:13.860 --> 12:15.310
Forget it.

12:18.860 --> 12:20.380
Let's go bring Motes home.

12:20.630 --> 12:23.850
I can't take any more controversy.

12:24.290 --> 12:27.050
I feel your pain, Landlady.

12:27.940 --> 12:31.440
But fear not, I, Schubert,

12:31.440 --> 12:34.020
will take him down first.

12:35.000 --> 12:37.480
I'll have my revenge for the gyoza

12:37.480 --> 12:39.280
I bought for Beethoven-senpai.

12:42.490 --> 12:44.990
Hamagonyaki

12:44.990 --> 12:47.490
Catch-a-Hamagon

12:47.490 --> 12:51.660
Yamano Shrine

12:48.200 --> 12:51.660
This is the mountain where
Hamagon is rumored to live.

12:51.660 --> 12:57.420
Hamagon Rolls

12:51.660 --> 12:57.420
Hamagon Sausages

12:52.080 --> 12:55.540
This area has been bustling
with people the past few days,

12:55.540 --> 12:57.420
all hoping to catch a glimpse of Hamagon.

12:59.790 --> 13:01.130
So close!

13:01.130 --> 13:02.640
One more, Pops.

13:03.220 --> 13:05.880
We're going to recover Motes and head home.

13:09.730 --> 13:12.390
The Forest King is mine!

13:13.390 --> 13:14.460
Tchaiko-chan...

13:14.460 --> 13:15.160
I smell it.

13:15.160 --> 13:16.430
I smell it.

13:16.750 --> 13:17.650
This way.

13:18.280 --> 13:20.110
My northern spirit...

13:20.110 --> 13:21.900
My Matagi blood is boiling!

13:22.530 --> 13:24.010
Tchaiko-chan...

13:24.490 --> 13:26.690
I can't keep up with you.

13:27.320 --> 13:28.630
Motes!

13:28.630 --> 13:30.070
Where are you?

13:30.070 --> 13:31.540
Come home.

13:31.540 --> 13:32.910
Motes!

13:33.140 --> 13:34.980
I'm not angry.

13:34.980 --> 13:36.790
Help me!

13:37.020 --> 13:39.290
Help me!

13:40.040 --> 13:41.000
A trap?

13:41.000 --> 13:44.090
I'm begging you, help me.

13:41.280 --> 13:43.200
No way, did Motes do this?

13:48.470 --> 13:51.060
It's the Curse of Hamagon!

13:51.060 --> 13:54.010
Damn it, Motes. What is he thinking?

13:59.790 --> 14:07.820
Maman!

14:08.110 --> 14:10.840
Hey, I hear something.

14:11.300 --> 14:12.560
I found them.

14:15.340 --> 14:16.960
The king of the mountain.

14:16.960 --> 14:18.680
Mushrooms!

14:18.680 --> 14:19.210
Huh?

14:19.210 --> 14:21.650
Oh, my God, oh, my God!

14:21.650 --> 14:23.150
I can't stop freaking out!

14:22.100 --> 14:24.440
Are you done with the Forest King already?

14:24.440 --> 14:26.630
You forgot that I love mushrooms?!

14:26.880 --> 14:29.550
Oh, man, oh, man.

14:28.220 --> 14:31.040
Tchaiko-chan, I can't keep up with you.

14:29.850 --> 14:31.640
Mushrooms!

14:36.030 --> 14:39.080
Please, Kanae, can we turn back?

14:39.080 --> 14:40.270
Don't be crazy.

14:40.810 --> 14:43.730
Motes! It's me!

14:43.950 --> 14:46.440
I'm here to take you home!

14:56.120 --> 14:56.870
Motes.

15:00.160 --> 15:01.380
Maman.

15:01.670 --> 15:03.280
What do you mean, "Maman"?

15:03.280 --> 15:04.400
What happened?

15:04.700 --> 15:06.280
Why are you doing this?

15:08.220 --> 15:10.050
Mama. Mama.

15:10.820 --> 15:11.730
Sousuke.

15:11.730 --> 15:12.900
Ma mama!

15:13.200 --> 15:15.370
Mamanma mama.

15:16.030 --> 15:17.050
Mamama!

15:17.410 --> 15:18.810
Mama!

15:19.150 --> 15:21.150
Mama!

15:22.580 --> 15:23.900
Get out of the mountains.

15:24.120 --> 15:26.250
You never said you could talk!

15:26.550 --> 15:28.820
This isn't your mountain, Motes.

15:29.250 --> 15:30.750
Let's go home.

15:33.310 --> 15:34.830
I'm the only one.

15:36.750 --> 15:40.290
Get out of the mountains!

15:43.830 --> 15:45.150
That was close, wasn't it?

15:45.600 --> 15:46.340
Over there.

15:54.140 --> 15:55.100
Stop!

16:01.230 --> 16:04.270
Be safe, my boy.

16:23.430 --> 16:25.540
Motes!

16:33.530 --> 16:37.180
Is that what this was all about?

16:43.330 --> 16:45.560
Hiking's fun for a change.

16:46.060 --> 16:48.320
What should I do?

17:02.870 --> 17:06.910
Ma-Maman's here.

17:11.840 --> 17:13.320
There, there.

17:27.140 --> 17:28.460
He's dead.

17:45.400 --> 17:46.490
Motes...

17:48.930 --> 17:50.260
Requiem.

17:53.570 --> 17:56.130
Fühle meine

17:57.360 --> 17:58.390
Musik!

18:10.850 --> 18:13.690
My melody is a requiem.

18:13.950 --> 18:16.950
The time has come to return to

18:17.530 --> 18:21.060
the pure, singular soul.

18:17.940 --> 18:21.940
Sparks fly from the flames

18:21.940 --> 18:27.980
Flames which I hope will burn my errors past

18:24.090 --> 18:25.370
Damn you, Mozart.

18:25.980 --> 18:29.490
I'm finally going to get my revenge.

18:38.200 --> 18:40.180
Holy crap!

18:38.680 --> 18:43.260
I look for you wherever I go

18:43.260 --> 18:45.220
It's Hamagon!

18:43.260 --> 18:55.280
Quiet is the room you left behind

18:45.220 --> 18:47.600
The Mountain King is angry!

18:55.130 --> 18:56.740
Wolf, again?

18:55.280 --> 19:02.900
I think of the moments I'll never have again

19:00.120 --> 19:01.230
Stop, Motes!

19:01.230 --> 19:02.450
Dude, this is bad!

19:02.900 --> 19:14.040
All I'm left with at night
is the thought of missing you

19:10.010 --> 19:10.620
Sousuke!

19:14.040 --> 19:19.340
I call for you, but get no answer

19:19.340 --> 19:22.580
Yet I search for you

19:19.510 --> 19:20.510
It's not hot.

19:21.360 --> 19:22.090
Really?

19:22.450 --> 19:24.710
Man, that scared me.

19:23.300 --> 19:27.460
Sparks fly from the flames

19:25.330 --> 19:28.450
But, I'm sorry.

19:27.460 --> 19:33.660
Flames which I hope will burn my errors past

19:28.840 --> 19:30.060
I'm sorry for being alive.

19:30.570 --> 19:33.560
I'm sorry for talking big
when I have no talent.

19:33.560 --> 19:34.570
Sousuke...

19:34.810 --> 19:35.950
I'm sorry.

19:35.950 --> 19:38.320
I'm sorry I can't keep up with Tchaiko-chan.

19:38.570 --> 19:39.670
I'm sorry.

19:39.670 --> 19:42.200
I'm sorry I act on my whims.

19:42.200 --> 19:44.910
I'm sorry for existing!

19:47.110 --> 19:49.200
All living mortals shall

19:49.200 --> 19:52.430
cower before my Musik and repent!

19:50.080 --> 19:52.080
I'm sorry. I don't even believe in
Bigfoot or monsters or anything.

19:52.430 --> 19:53.830
I'm sorry for ripping people off.

19:54.100 --> 19:57.030
Burn in the flames of grief.

19:57.030 --> 19:59.340
Repent, repent,

19:57.120 --> 20:05.320
Try as I may to bring back the past

19:59.340 --> 20:02.300
repent forever!

20:05.840 --> 20:15.720
All that comes is my desire to see you

20:13.020 --> 20:14.250
More.

20:14.250 --> 20:15.730
Requiem!

20:15.720 --> 20:18.720
I call for you, but—

20:16.000 --> 20:18.730
Requiem for the world!

20:20.740 --> 20:22.310
That's enough.

20:25.560 --> 20:28.060
Beethes. Why are you here?

20:28.610 --> 20:30.060
Why are you okay?

20:32.030 --> 20:34.630
What do I have to repent?

20:36.000 --> 20:37.590
Not a single thing.

20:40.220 --> 20:41.600
You have loads.

21:04.860 --> 21:06.640
Is this the cause?

21:06.640 --> 21:07.780
Looks like it.

21:20.430 --> 21:22.690
H-How?

21:22.690 --> 21:23.780
I see.

21:24.080 --> 21:26.720
It must have just been passed out in shock.

21:30.610 --> 21:31.600
My boy!

21:33.780 --> 21:36.220
My boy!

21:41.340 --> 21:42.480
Why?

21:42.480 --> 21:45.400
He must have been, y'know,

21:45.400 --> 21:47.860
he must have been surprised and stuff.

21:47.860 --> 21:50.150
He's probably going through
his rebellious phase.

22:00.870 --> 22:03.390
Ah, oh well.

22:09.040 --> 22:10.020
Wonderful.

22:10.430 --> 22:12.430
It's love!

22:12.850 --> 22:16.840
There has to be something wrong with you
to want to become a mother deer, though.

22:19.450 --> 22:20.790
It's from Cho-chan.

22:21.690 --> 22:24.150
Indeed, first it was Hamagon,

22:21.690 --> 22:26.200
Terror!
Hamamatsu Urban Legend II

22:24.150 --> 22:26.200
and now we learn of yet
another mystery creature.

22:26.950 --> 22:28.320
We call it

22:28.320 --> 22:31.900
Hamassie, and we will
pursue it going forward.

22:32.200 --> 22:34.940
Maman!

22:34.940 --> 22:35.450
Huh?

22:38.790 --> 22:40.890
I don't care anymore.

22:43.000 --> 22:46.000
To be continued

24:15.970 --> 24:27.320
08: "Girls' Night Out"

24:16.420 --> 24:19.600
The girls' night out:
An exciting, fun, hearty time.

24:19.600 --> 24:22.080
A girls' night out of girls,
for girls, by girls.

24:22.080 --> 24:23.840
Ah, how glorious it is,
the girls' night out.

24:23.840 --> 24:26.400
So anyway, there's a
girls' night out, but,

24:26.400 --> 24:28.980
like, is this even a
girls' night out?
